+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+In confirmed MAIN standby, a fresh gas press of at least 0.1s and release requests SET−/release/SET−/release regardless of engagement or lateral activity. Send the second press even after first engagement, which can lower set speed by one step. Each release permits at most one pair; failed engagement does not repeat the same cue. Brake, CANCEL, MAIN OFF, renewed gas, driver buttons, lost eligibility or cancellation stop the remainder. Cancellation takes priority; normal speed buttons resume after the sequence.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+While parked, update both host and Panda and restart with MAIN OFF, then press MAIN ON after boot. Initial MAIN OFF is independent of AutoEngage. Another pair requires three seconds after the last TX and a fresh pedal cycle; blocked/expired cues are not queued. Option OFF revokes permission while preserving MAIN tracking.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+Each press is at most three frames/60ms, separated by about 80ms, completing in about 0.2s. Panda checks six frames total, at least 60ms of release and a 240ms envelope. Retain 0.5s MAIN settling, initial target/dashboard 30–160km/h and existing wheel/input/driver-priority guards. Absolute MAIN state is not decoded; standby already ON at restart needs a MAIN-OFF restart or actual stock ON from physical SET for synchronization. TX echo is not acceptance; no direct braking, stopping, standstill launch or ECU acceptance guarantee is provided.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
